by ousamabenyounes at 2026-04-18T21:59:21Z

Good catch, thanks. From inside the middleware there's no way to tell retry from failure — routing happens after `next()` throws.

Clean split: keep the middleware fix (plugs the `finally` race on retry), add a listener on `WorkerMessageFailedEvent` that releases the lock when `!willRetry()` and the envelope carries a `DeduplicateStamp`. That covers the failed-transport path.

Happy to push that on top here, or split to a follow-up if you prefer this PR narrow.

