by ousamabenyounes at 2026-04-22T21:13:28Z

Thanks for the review @GromNaN, @VincentLanglet — agreed on the split, middleware can't tell retry from failure from inside `handle()` so the lock release belongs on the failure event.

Pushed `dbea108`: new `ReleaseDeduplicationLockOnFailureListener` on `WorkerMessageFailedEvent` at priority 0 (runs after `SendFailedMessageForRetryListener` at 100, so `willRetry()` is set). It releases the lock only when `!willRetry()`, a `DeduplicateStamp` is present, and `!onlyDeduplicateInQueue` (that path is already released at the consumer step by the middleware). Wired in `FrameworkBundle` under `messenger.failure.*`, removed alongside the dedup middleware when the Lock component is disabled. CHANGELOG updated and 5 unit tests cover the four branches + priority ordering.
